IMPORT prelude

-- Transfer of Land Act 1893 (Western Australia) -- what registration does and what makes the registered title paramount
-- (ss 52(2), 53, 58, 68, 134, 199, 201, 214A), what a registered mortgage is and how a lender reaches the land on default
-- (ss 105, 105AA, 106, 107, 108), and joint proprietors, "no survivorship" and the survivor's registration on a death
-- (ss 60, 61, 187, 227).
--
-- Edition: compilation from legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 49493, retrieved 7 September 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49493.txt. The deposit names no compilation number; its compilation table ends with the
-- Petroleum Legislation Amendment Act 2024 Pt 5 Div 13 (other than s 424(4)), in force 28 May 2026, and the last reprint listed is
-- Reprint 11 as at 8 January 2016. The uncommenced provisions table lists the Transfer of Land Amendment Act 2003 ss 43, 46, 56,
-- 57, the Community Titles Act 2018 s 253, the Petroleum Legislation Amendment Act 2024 s 424(4) and the Evidence Act 2025
-- s 492(2); none is shown or encoded.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement au/wa:REQ-0007 (priority 1), raised 7 times by the three Western Australian cradle-to-grave lives:
-- Chloe c052 (settlement of the Byford land, the mortgage, title registered: "What makes the title indefeasible; what does the
-- lender register?", ss 68, 105), c081 (the Baldivis townhouse, s 68), c087 (her father Graham dies; the Armadale house by
-- survivorship, s 60), c096 (Liam dies; the apartment by survivorship, s 60); Jake k076 (settlement of his apartment, s 68);
-- Daniel d074 (his father dies; s 60) and d093 (Daniel dies; the house to Priya by survivorship, s 60). SCOPED to those
-- provisions and the ones immediately needed to answer them: when an instrument is registered and what it passes (ss 52(2),
-- 53, 58), the exceptions to paramountcy (s 68(1), (1A)), notice of unregistered interests (s 134), recovery actions and
-- compensation (ss 199, 201, 214A), the mortgage's form, signature and effect and the default procedure (ss 105-108), and the
-- survivor's and the executor's routes onto the register (ss 61, 187, 227).
--
-- Not encoded: bringing land under the Act (Part II), Crown land (s 68(2)-(4) and every Crown land qualification), leases,
-- easements and covenants beyond s 68(1A), caveats (Part IV Div 3), the mortgagee's sale proceeds, foreclosure and remedies
-- (ss 109-119), the conditional tenure land qualification to ss 106-108 (Land Administration Act 1997 Part 6 Div 2), the
-- Registrar's and Commissioner's powers and fees, electronic conveyancing beyond s 105AA, and the Community Titles Act 2018 and
-- Strata Titles Act 1985 (which c081 and k076 also ask about). The approved forms are not in the deposit. What "fraud" means in
-- s 68 is not defined by the Act and is an input. The right of survivorship itself -- that a surviving joint tenant takes the
-- whole -- is NOT stated anywhere in the deposited text (see s 60 below); this encoding asserts only what the Act says.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Transfer of Land Act 1893 -- title, mortgage and survivorship`

§§ `52(2), 53, 58 -- registration, priority, and nothing passes until registered`

-- s 52(2): an instrument affecting land with a registered certificate "is registered when a memorandum referred to in section 56
-- in relation to the original instrument has been entered in the Register on the certificate".
-- s 58: "No instrument until registered in manner herein provided shall be effectual to pass any estate or interest in any land
-- under the operation of this Act or to render such land liable to any mortgage or charge ... but upon such registration the
-- estate or interest comprised in the instrument shall pass or as the case may be the land shall become liable".
GIVEN `a memorandum of the instrument is entered in the Register on the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument passes the estate or interest` IF
    `a memorandum of the instrument is entered in the Register on the certificate`

-- s 53(1): the Registrar registers instruments "in the order, and from the time, of its presentation".
-- s 53(2): instruments affecting the same estate or interest "have priority as between each other according to the time of
-- registration and not according to the date of the instrument, notwithstanding any actual or constructive notice".
-- Neither the date of the instruments nor notice is a parameter, because s 53(2) says neither counts.
GIVEN `time the first instrument was registered` IS A NUMBER, `time the second instrument was registered` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first instrument has priority` IF
    `time the first instrument was registered` LESS THAN `time the second instrument was registered`

§§ `68, 134 -- the estate of the registered proprietor is paramount`

-- s 68(1): the registered proprietor "shall except in case of fraud hold the same subject to such encumbrances as may be notified
-- on the registered certificate of title for the land; but absolutely free from all other encumbrances whatsoever except the
-- estate or interest of a proprietor claiming the same land under a prior registered certificate of title and except as regards
-- any portion of land that may by wrong description of parcels or boundaries be included in the certificate ... not being a
-- purchaser for valuable consideration or deriving from or through such a purchaser."
-- s 68(1A): "Despite subsection (1)" the land is deemed subject to reservations, exceptions, conditions and powers in the grant,
-- "any rights subsisting under any adverse possession", "any public rights of way", "any easements acquired by enjoyment or user
-- or subsisting over or upon or affecting such land", "any unpaid rates", "any mining lease or licence issued under the
-- provisions of any statute", and "any prior unregistered lease or agreement for lease or for letting for a term not exceeding 5
-- years to a tenant in actual possession" -- "notwithstanding the same respectively may not be specially notified".
-- s 134: a person taking a transfer from a registered proprietor is not "affected by notice actual or constructive of any trust
-- or unregistered interest ... and the knowledge that any such trust or unregistered interest is in existence shall not of
-- itself be imputed as fraud." s 55(1): the Registrar does not enter trusts on a certificate (with exceptions for trusts in the
-- Crown grant or transfer).
-- "Fraud" is not defined in the Act; whether there was fraud is an input. In case of fraud, s 68 gives no freedom from anything.
DECLARE Interest IS ONE OF
    `an encumbrance notified on the certificate`
    `the estate of a proprietor under a prior registered certificate for the same land`
    `a reservation or condition in the Crown grant`
    `rights under adverse possession`
    `a public right of way`
    `an easement acquired by enjoyment or user`
    `unpaid rates`
    `a mining lease or licence issued under a statute`
    `an unregistered mortgage`
    `an unregistered interest the proprietor knew of`
    `a trust not entered on the certificate`

GIVEN `the interest` IS AN Interest
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the interest binds the registered proprietor despite section 68` IF
    CONSIDER `the interest`
    WHEN `an unregistered mortgage` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an unregistered interest the proprietor knew of` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a trust not entered on the certificate` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the interest` IS AN Interest, `the registered proprietor's title is a case of fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 68 frees the registered proprietor from the interest` IF
        (NOT `the registered proprietor's title is a case of fraud`)
    AND (NOT `the interest binds the registered proprietor despite section 68` `the interest`)

-- s 68(1A), the short lease: binding though unregistered only if prior, for a term "not exceeding 5 years", and to "a tenant in
-- actual possession". A registered lease is a notified encumbrance under s 68(1). The proviso: "no option of purchase or renewal
-- in any such lease or agreement shall be valid as against a subsequent registered interest unless such lease or agreement is
-- registered or protected by caveat."
GIVEN `the lease is registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `the lease is prior to the proprietor's interest` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `term of the lease in years` IS A NUMBER, `the tenant is in actual possession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registered proprietor takes subject to the lease` IF
        `the lease is registered`
    OR  (    `the lease is prior to the proprietor's interest`
         AND `term of the lease in years` AT MOST 5
         AND `the tenant is in actual possession`)

GIVEN `the lease is registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `the lease is protected by caveat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an option in the lease is valid against a later registered interest` IF
    `the lease is registered` OR `the lease is protected by caveat`

-- s 68(1), wrong description: land included in a certificate by wrong description of parcels or boundaries is protected only
-- for a proprietor who is "a purchaser for valuable consideration or deriving from or through such a purchaser".
GIVEN `the proprietor is a purchaser for valuable consideration or derives through one` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 68 protects land included by wrong description` IF
    `the proprietor is a purchaser for valuable consideration or derives through one`

§§ `199, 201, 214A -- recovering the land, compensation, and fraud`

-- s 199: "Subject to sections 68 and 81T, no action of ejectment or other action for the recovery of any land shall lie or be
-- sustained against the person registered as proprietor" except: (a) a mortgagee against a mortgagor in default; (b) an
-- annuitant against a grantor in default; (c) a lessor against a lessee in default; (d) "a person deprived of any land by fraud
-- as against the person registered as proprietor of such land through fraud or as against a person deriving otherwise than as a
-- transferee bona fide for value from or through a person so registered through fraud"; (e) misdescription, against a registered
-- proprietor "not being a transferee thereof bona fide for value"; (f) a proprietor under a certificate "prior in date of
-- registration". Otherwise the certificate "shall be held in every court to be an absolute bar and estoppel".
-- s 202: a "purchaser bona fide for valuable consideration" is not left subject to ejectment or damages because the proprietor
-- through whom he claims was registered through fraud or error.
DECLARE RecoveryClaim IS ONE OF
    `a mortgagee against a mortgagor in default`
    `a lessor against a lessee in default`
    `a person deprived by fraud against the proprietor registered through that fraud`
    `a person deprived by fraud against a later transferee bona fide for value`
    `a misdescription claimant against a proprietor who is not a bona fide transferee for value`
    `a misdescription claimant against a bona fide transferee for value`
    `a proprietor under an earlier registered certificate for the same land`
    `a person with an unregistered interest`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A RecoveryClaim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an action to recover the land lies against the registered proprietor` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a person deprived by fraud against a later transferee bona fide for value` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a misdescription claimant against a bona fide transferee for value` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a person with an unregistered interest` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 201(1): a person deprived of land or an interest "in consequence of fraud or through the bringing of such land under the
-- operation of this Act or by the registration of any other person as proprietor ... or in consequence of any error or
-- misdescription" may sue the person who applied or acquired title through it. (2): outside fraud and the person's own error,
-- a bona fide transfer for value caps that person's liability at the consideration received. (3): "In such lastmentioned case and
-- also in case the person against whom such action for damages is directed to be brought as aforesaid shall be dead or shall
-- have been adjudged bankrupt or cannot be found within the jurisdiction of the Supreme Court" damages and costs "may be
-- recovered from the State by action against the Registrar as nominal defendant". (5): later buildings and improvements are
-- excluded from the damages.
GIVEN `the claimant was deprived by fraud, registration, error or misdescription` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the person liable is dead` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person liable is bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the person liable cannot be found within the jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the person liable's liability is capped by a bona fide transfer for value under section 201(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `damages may be recovered from the State` IF
        `the claimant was deprived by fraud, registration, error or misdescription`
    AND (    `the person liable is dead`
         OR  `the person liable is bankrupt`
         OR  `the person liable cannot be found within the jurisdiction`
         OR  `the person liable's liability is capped by a bona fide transfer for value under section 201(2)`)

-- s 214A: "Any certificate of title, instrument, entry, erasure or alteration procured or made by fraud in any of the
-- circumstances set out in section 214 is void as against all persons who are party to that fraud, whether or not anyone is
-- convicted of that fraud." Conviction is therefore not a parameter.
GIVEN `procured by fraud in a section 214 circumstance` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person was party to the fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate or instrument is void against the person` IF
    `procured by fraud in a section 214 circumstance` AND `the person was party to the fraud`

§§ `105, 105AA, 106 -- the mortgage: form, signature, effect`

-- s 105(1): the proprietor "may -- (a) mortgage the land; or (b) charge the land with the payment of an annuity." (2): "A mortgage
-- or charge shall be in an approved form." The Act does not say what follows from a mortgage not in an approved form.
-- s 105(3), (4): if the counterpart lodged "purports to be signed by the person who, on registration ... will become the
-- proprietor of the mortgage" but "does not purport to be signed by the proprietor of the land", no counterpart signed by the
-- proprietor of the land is also lodged, and the instrument is registered, then "the mortgage or charge is not valid or binding
-- against the proprietor of the land unless, before the charging instrument was registered, the proprietor of the land signed a
-- counterpart". (5): "Subsection (4) overrides section 58."
DECLARE Mortgage HAS
    `registered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a lodged counterpart is signed by the mortgagee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a lodged counterpart is signed by the proprietor of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proprietor of the land signed a counterpart before registration` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the mortgage` IS A Mortgage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 105(4) applies` IF
        `the mortgage`'s `registered`
    AND `the mortgage`'s `a lodged counterpart is signed by the mortgagee`
    AND (NOT `the mortgage`'s `a lodged counterpart is signed by the proprietor of the land`)

GIVEN `the mortgage` IS A Mortgage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mortgage binds the proprietor of the land` IF
        `the mortgage`'s `registered`
    AND (    (NOT `section 105(4) applies` `the mortgage`)
         OR  `the mortgage`'s `the proprietor of the land signed a counterpart before registration`)

-- s 105AA: "A mortgage must not be lodged electronically under the Electronic Conveyancing Act 2014 unless the mortgagee -- (a) has
-- signed the mortgage instrument; and (b) holds a counterpart of the mortgage instrument signed by the proprietor of the land."
GIVEN `the mortgagee has signed the mortgage instrument` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the mortgagee holds a counterpart signed by the proprietor of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mortgage may be lodged electronically` IF
    `the mortgagee has signed the mortgage instrument` AND `the mortgagee holds a counterpart signed by the proprietor of the land`

-- s 106(1): a mortgage "shall when registered ... have effect as a security but shall not operate as a transfer of the land thereby
-- mortgaged". (Subject to Land Administration Act 1997 Part 6 Div 2 for conditional tenure land: not encoded.)
DECLARE MortgageEffect IS ONE OF
    `a security over the land`
    `a transfer of the land`

GIVEN `the effect` IS A MortgageEffect
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a registered mortgage operates as` IF
    CONSIDER `the effect`
    WHEN `a security over the land` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `106, 107, 108 -- default, notice, and the power of sale`

-- s 106(1): if default in payment or in a covenant "be continued for one month or for such other period of time as may therein
-- for that purpose be expressly fixed" the mortgagee "may serve on the mortgagor ... notice in writing to pay".
-- s 108: if the default continues "for one month after the service of such notice or for such other period as may in such
-- mortgage or charge be for that purpose fixed" the mortgagee "may sell the land mortgaged". The Act counts in months; a period
-- fixed by the mortgage is entered in months, 0 meaning none fixed.
GIVEN `months fixed by the mortgage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`months the default must continue` MEANS
    IF `months fixed by the mortgage` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `months fixed by the mortgage`
    ELSE 1

GIVEN `the mortgage is registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `months the default has continued` IS A NUMBER,
      `months fixed by the mortgage for notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mortgagee may serve a notice to pay` IF
        `the mortgage is registered`
    AND `months the default has continued` AT LEAST `months the default must continue` `months fixed by the mortgage for notice`

-- s 106(2): service "is not properly effected unless" the notice is (a) "delivered personally"; (b) "sent by registered post" to
-- (i) the address entered in the Register or (ii) the address known to the mortgagee as the current address; (c) "left in a
-- conspicuous place on the mortgaged or charged land"; or (d) sent "in compliance with a way of sending notices electronically
-- (for example, to an email address) that is prescribed by the regulations". s 106(3) keeps facsimile service for those who
-- elected it before 7 August 2023: not encoded.
DECLARE ServiceMethod IS ONE OF
    `delivered personally`
    `registered post to the address in the Register`
    `registered post to the known current address`
    `left in a conspicuous place on the land`
    `an electronic way prescribed by the regulations`
    `ordinary post`
    `an email by a way not prescribed`

GIVEN `the method` IS A ServiceMethod
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice is properly served` IF
    CONSIDER `the method`
    WHEN `ordinary post` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an email by a way not prescribed` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 107: where money secured "is made payable on demand a demand in writing pursuant to the mortgage shall be equivalent to the
-- notice in writing to pay ... and no other notice shall be required".
GIVEN `the money is payable on demand` IS A BOOLEAN, `a written demand was made under the mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the method` IS A ServiceMethod, `a notice to pay was served` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months the default continued after the notice or demand` IS A NUMBER, `months fixed by the mortgage for sale` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mortgagee may sell the land` IF
        (    (`the money is payable on demand` AND `a written demand was made under the mortgage`)
         OR  (`a notice to pay was served` AND `the notice is properly served` `the method`))
    AND `months the default continued after the notice or demand` AT LEAST `months the default must continue` `months fixed by the mortgage for sale`

§§ `60, 61 -- joint proprietors and "no survivorship"`

-- s 60: "Two or more persons who may be registered as joint proprietors of land shall be deemed to be entitled to the same as
-- joint tenants; and in all cases where 2 or more persons are entitled as tenants in common to undivided shares of or in any land
-- such persons may receive one certificate for the entirety or separate certificates for the undivided shares."
-- That is all s 60 says. It deems joint proprietors joint tenants; it does not itself say that the survivor takes the whole.
-- The lives cite s 60 for survivorship; survivorship is the general-law incident of a joint tenancy (an inference, not text).
DECLARE Holding IS ONE OF
    `as joint proprietors`
    `as tenants in common in undivided shares`
    `as sole proprietor`

GIVEN `the holding` IS A Holding, `number registered` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proprietors are deemed joint tenants` IF
        `number registered` AT LEAST 2
    AND CONSIDER `the holding`
        WHEN `as joint proprietors` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the holding` IS A Holding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `separate certificates may issue for undivided shares` IF
    CONSIDER `the holding`
    WHEN `as tenants in common in undivided shares` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 61(1), (2): "no survivorship" may be endorsed on a transfer or lease to joint proprietors, or entered at their written
-- direction. (3): once signed by the Registrar "it shall not be lawful for any persons other than the proprietors registered to
-- transfer or otherwise deal with the property without the order of the Supreme Court or a judge thereof ... or the order of the
-- Commissioner." The section does not say that the words convert the joint tenancy into a tenancy in common or end survivorship;
-- what it says is who may deal without an order.
GIVEN `"no survivorship" has been signed by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person is a registered proprietor` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Supreme Court or the Commissioner has ordered it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may lawfully deal with the property` IF
        (NOT `"no survivorship" has been signed by the Registrar`)
    OR  `the person is a registered proprietor`
    OR  `the Supreme Court or the Commissioner has ordered it`

§§ `227, 187 -- onto the register after a death`

-- s 227: "Upon the death of any person registered with any other person as joint proprietor of any land ... the Commissioner on
-- the application of the person entitled and proof to his satisfaction of such events as aforesaid may direct the Registrar to
-- register such applicant as the proprietor thereof; and she or he shall upon being registered ... become the transferee of such
-- land ... and be deemed its proprietor." "The person entitled" is not defined; it is an input. The section needs no probate.
GIVEN `the deceased was registered under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `the deceased's holding` IS A Holding,
      `the applicant is the person entitled` IS A BOOLEAN, `the death is proved to the Commissioner's satisfaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner may direct the survivor's registration under section 227` IF
        `the deceased was registered under this Act`
    AND `the applicant is the person entitled`
    AND `the death is proved to the Commissioner's satisfaction`
    AND CONSIDER `the deceased's holding`
        WHEN `as joint proprietors` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 187(1): on receipt of an office copy of probate or letters of administration, and "on an application in writing of the
-- executor, administrator, or Public Trustee", the Registrar "shall" enter the appointment, and the legal personal representative
-- becomes "the transferee and be deemed to be the proprietor of the estate or interest of the deceased proprietor"; (2) the title
-- relates back to the death; (3) where probate or administration is granted to more than one person "all of them for the time
-- being shall join and concur in every dealing".
GIVEN `the Registrar has an office copy of the probate or letters` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the representative applied in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must register the legal personal representative under section 187` IF
    `the Registrar has an office copy of the probate or letters` AND `the representative applied in writing`

GIVEN `representatives granted probate or administration` IS A NUMBER, `representatives joining in the dealing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the representatives may deal with the land` IF
    `representatives joining in the dealing` AT LEAST `representatives granted probate or administration`
